<description>
resolves #29618.

This PR adds a config flag option `-v2onlyclearnet` which disallows outbound v1 connections on ipv4 and ipv6 networks since they're unencrypted. outbound v1 connections are still possible from tor/i2p/cjdns peers since they're encrypted networks.

- v1 outbound connections to peers are not attempted
- v1 reconnections are not attempted (if peer is falsely advertised as v2 peer and we attempt a v2 connection but it fails, we do not attempt a v1 reconnection when `-v2onlyclearnet` is switched on)

Currently 70% of reachable nodes in network supporting v2 (according to https://21.ninja/reachable-nodes/node-service-share/ and https://bitnodes.io/nodes). Also found 81% of addresses supporting v2 in the addrman of nodes I checked - personal node and the nodes in [peer.observer](https://peer.observer/addrman/alice). (You can use [this branch ](https://github.com/stratospher/bitcoin/commits/addrinfo_service_display/)to check the % of v2 addresses in a node's addrman.)

EDIT: see [summary](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/30951#issuecomment-4346061700) on pros and cons for whether to allow v2 inbounds or not for `-v2onlyclearnet`.
</description>

<commits>
c763a476fc net: add helper to identify clearnet networks

only-clearnet condition is used in a few other places as well.

172bbfcb16 net: add option in CConnman to allow only v2 clearnet connections

a boolean option `m_v2only_clearnet` is introduced in CConnman which
will (in a later commit) store if the user wishes to establish only
outbound/inbound v2 connections to IPv4/IPv6 peers since they are
unencrypted.

this option is accessible outside CConnman using `RequiresV2Peer()`.
it takes a network rather than an address because an inbound Tor peer
arrives from a loopback address, so only `ConnectedThroughNetwork()`
knows it came over onion.

5753b99896 net: add RequiresV2Dest() for name proxy destinations

when bitcoind delegates DNS to a name proxy (ex: Tor), the destination
is left unresolved and `GetNetClass()` reports NET_UNROUTABLE - same as
a LAN peer. outbound callers (in a later commit) use this instead of
`RequiresV2Peer()` so those destinations require v2 instead of being
allowed to be v1.

66ab292f9d init: add -v2onlyclearnet config option

if this option is set by the user, v1 connections to and from IPv4/IPv6
peers will be disallowed. only users with a real need should turn it on:
in the very unlikely event that everyone did, v1 nodes would struggle to
find honest peers and become easier to eclipse.

4fb0aadce0 net: disable v1 connections, reconnections on clearnet

if `-v2onlyclearnet` is turned on,
- v1 addresses from addrman are dropped if selected and manual
connections aren't attempted for outbound connections if it's
from IPV4/IPV6 networks.
- v1 downgrade mechanism is not attempted if v2 connection wasn't
successful.
- if a v1 inbound clearnet peer connects to us, we disconnect it
during version processing.

2ac3b16830 log: v1 disconnects due to -v2onlyclearnet

c15768fad0 test: Check that v1 connections to clearnet peers don't work

when `-v2onlyclearnet` is turned on, for outbound connections:
- v1 connections to clearnet peers don't work
- v2 connections to clearnet peers work
- v1 connections to tor/i2p/cjdns peer works

a proxy is used because otherwise NET_UNROUTABLE is the default
network in the tests.

for inbound connections:
kept a unit test which can be removed if reviewers think otherwise
because the source of an inbound in the functional tests is always
127.0.0.1.

2f443a4eed doc: add release notes for v2onlyclearnet option
</commits>

